## 2. User types and permissions

The platform should have four main user types.

1\. Super Admin — Your company

- Creates and manages colleges.
- Generates unique college IDs.
- Creates faculty accounts.
- Activates or deactivates accounts.
- Monitors platform usage and technical errors.
- Manages public college listings and approved rankings.

  2\. College / Institution
- Has a unique college identity.
- Has faculty accounts assigned to it.
- Can view institution-level reports if this permission is enabled.
- Cannot access another college's private student records.

  3\. Faculty
- Logs in with credentials supplied by the administrator.
- Connects their own Google account.
- Creates examinations and questions.
- Generates test links.
- Views results, rankings, and malpractice review evidence.
- Downloads or accesses reports saved to their Drive.

  4\. Student
- Opens the examination link.
- Enters name and roll number.
- Reads instructions.
- Takes the exam.
- Submits answers.
- Receives a result if the faculty has enabled student result visibility.

Access rule: Every record must be connected to the correct college, faculty, and examination. A faculty member must never be able to access another faculty member's private examination data just by changing an ID in the browser or API request.

