The student should see a clean, distraction-free examination screen.

### Interface elements

- Examination title.
- Countdown timer.
- Question number.
- Question text and images.
- Answer area.
- Next and Previous buttons.
- Question navigation.
- Save status.
- Submit button.

### Important behaviour

- Save answers periodically and when the student navigates between questions.
- Preserve answers if the page reloads or the network briefly disconnects.
- Prevent submission after the server-side deadline.
- Show a confirmation before final submission.
- Automatically submit or close the examination when time expires, according to the configured examination rules.

For coding questions, we should later decide whether students will execute code in a secure sandbox. Never execute arbitrary student code directly on the Django application server.

## 10. English speaking assessment

Specialized assessment feature

This feature should evaluate not only what a student says but also how they communicate.

[E-SPK — Evaluación de pronunciación en inglés con IA (3 minutos)](https://images.openai.com/static-rsc-4/tBJRvB3G_BjjIGwJ-dYTFy8pcK3wIFd0R5E7x0P2h_SkVDzqsmGZM6V4aRynZq-4ilxiEZNgAasL0ogo7sV2fm8nlWjuWPXIGe7Mv3YDz_xKqSnxC_LpmaoBskpLn5tMAngd8PcexFCTWwb3xOxViDqLegxCRJimojwgog1l8es?purpose=inline)

[espkcert.com](https://www.espkcert.com/?utm_source=chatgpt.com)

### Proposed examination structure

Three situation-based tasks:

| Task | Difficulty | Situation                                                                                |
| ---- | ---------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| 1    | Easy       | You lost your railway ticket. Explain how you would ask for assistance at the station.   |
| 2    | Medium     | You purchased a damaged product. Explain the problem and request a suitable solution.    |
| 3    | Medium     | You need to organize a college event with limited time and resources. Explain your plan. |

Each task can have a three-minute limit, subject to your final examination rules.

### Recording workflow

1. Student sees the situation.
2. Student reads the instructions.
3. Browser requests microphone permission.
4. Student records their response.
5. Student can make up to three attempts.
6. Student listens to the recordings.
7. Student selects one recording.
8. Student clicks Submit.
9. Only the selected recording is evaluated.

Do not automatically select the highest-scoring recording. The student should select which attempt to submit.

### Technologies

| Technology         | Function                               |
| ------------------ | -------------------------------------- |
| MediaRecorder API  | Record student voice                   |
| faster-whisper     | Convert audio into text                |
| Ollama + local LLM | Evaluate response content              |
| librosa            | Extract audio features                 |
| Silero VAD         | Detect speech and silence              |
| Celery             | Run audio processing in the background |

### Assessment dimensions

A possible 10-mark rubric:

| Category                    | Marks |
| --------------------------- | ----- |
| Understanding and relevance | 3     |
| Grammar                     | 2     |
| Vocabulary                  | 1     |
| Fluency                     | 2     |
| Clarity and intelligibility | 2     |
| Total                       | 10    |

There is an important technical limitation: speech-to-text alone cannot reliably assess pronunciation. Audio analysis can measure pauses, speaking time and speaking rate, but these are not the same as pronunciation quality.

Therefore:

- Use the transcript to evaluate content, grammar and vocabulary.
- Use audio features to support fluency assessment.
- Do not penalize a student's Indian English accent.
- Mark uncertain pronunciation or clarity scores for faculty review until the scoring model has been validated.
- Do not interpret speech-recognition mistakes as student grammar mistakes.

### AI evaluation output

The AI service should return structured data, for example:

```
{
  "relevance_score": 2.5,
  "grammar_score": 1.5,
  "vocabulary_score": 0.8,
  "fluency_score": 1.5,
  "clarity_score": null,
  "total_score": 6.3,
  "review_required": true,
  "feedback": [
    "The response addresses the situation.",
    "Try using more complete sentences."
  ]
}
```

The total should be calculated from the valid scored categories only, with a clearly defined rule for any category awaiting human review. The example above is illustrative, not a fixed scoring algorithm.

## 11. Automatic evaluation for other questions

Different question types need different evaluation methods.

| Question type        | Evaluation method                                  |
| -------------------- | -------------------------------------------------- |
| MCQ                  | Compare answer against answer key                  |
| Short answer         | Rubric-based AI evaluation                         |
| Descriptive answer   | AI evaluation against faculty marking rubric       |
| English speaking     | Transcript and audio analysis                      |
| Programming          | Test cases in a secure execution environment       |
| Situational question | AI evaluates relevance, reasoning and completeness |

### Recommended evaluation architecture

Django should send evaluation tasks to Celery workers.

The AI evaluation service should receive:

- Question.
- Student answer.
- Expected answer or marking rubric.
- Maximum marks.
- Evaluation instructions.

It should return:

- Marks.
- Reason for the marks.
- Strengths.
- Improvement suggestions.
- Review-required status.
- Model and rubric version.

Very important: AI-generated marks should be treated as provisional until the faculty-approved validation process establishes that the evaluation is sufficiently reliable for the intended examination.

